# Services / API

## Income

- `salary_pay_period` and `income_for_pay_period` own month attribution
- Overview exposes current pay-period income; MoM % and 6-month series for the modal
- Do not treat generic credits or transfers as income

## Classify

- Single: `PATCH /api/transactions/{id}/classify`
- Bulk: `POST /api/transactions/classify-bulk`
- Exclude non-transaction emails: `POST /api/transactions/exclude` → `transaction_type=not_a_transaction`, `excludes_from_spending`, clear review; linked email marked `skipped`
- Side effects by category (transfer → `is_transfer` + exclude from spending; income type updates, etc.)
- User classify clears `needs_review` and sets `user_verified`

## Persistence

- Prefer additive schema changes; keep fingerprints / idempotent sync intact
- Avoid rewriting unrelated enrichment when fixing one field
